/-!
# Where the reading of a section at a scheme point vanishes

Let `X` be an algebraic space, `M` an invertible `𝒪_X`-module, `σ` a global section of `M` and
`k : h_T ⟶ X` a morphism from a scheme of the site. The reading of `σ` along `k`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.pointGlobalSection`, a global section of the invertible module
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.pointModule` on `T`) vanishes at a point `t ∈ T` exactly when `t` lies in
the base change `Z(σ) ×_X T` of the zero scheme of `σ` (Stacks 0845), that is, exactly when the
image of `t` in `|X|` lies in `|Z(σ)|`.

On an affine `T` the closed subscheme `Z(σ) ×_X T` is the zero scheme of the inverse image `k^*σ`
on `h_T` read at the identity chart (`k⁻¹Z(σ) = Z(k^*σ)`, and the defining ideal of a zero scheme
at an affine chart is the evaluation ideal of the section), and that evaluation ideal is the
ideal of the scheme-level zero scheme of the reading, through the identification of the sections
of `k^*M` over the identity chart with the global sections of the reading. The scheme-level
statement `AlgebraicGeometry.mem_nonvanishingLocus_iff_notMem_supportSet_zeroScheme` concludes.
A general `T` is covered by affine opens, along which both sides are compatible with base change.

This is the input of the proof that families of curves are étale locally schemes (Stacks 0E6F)
which reads where the canonical section of `𝒪(D)` vanishes on a fibre.

## Main results

* `Space.modulePullbackSections_eq_globalSectionsPullbackMap`: the two
  spellings of the inverse image of a global section agree.
* `Space.chartKer_zeroScheme_ideal_top_eq`: the chart ideal of a zero scheme
  along a scheme point of an affine scheme.
* `Space.mem_nonvanishingLocus_pointGlobalSection_iff_notMem_supportSet_chartKer`:
  the reading vanishes exactly on the base change of the zero scheme.
* `Space.notMem_nonvanishingLocus_pointGlobalSection_iff_mem_subspacePointSet`:
  the same in terms of the points of `X`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0845](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0845)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0846](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0846)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CY)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite
open Stacks.Cohomology.SiteModules (globalSectionsFunctor)
open Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor (ringSheaf)

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

local notation "𝒯" => BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS

/-- **The two spellings of the inverse image of a global section agree**: the one through the
comparison `𝒪_{Y'} ≅ g^*𝒪_Y` and `SheafOfModules.unitHomEquiv`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.modulePullbackSections`) and the one through the unit of `g^* ⊣ g_*`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.globalSectionsPullbackMap`). -/
theorem modulePullbackSections_eq_globalSectionsPullbackMap {Y Y' : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS}
    (g : Y' ⟶ Y) (N : Modules.{u, u} B S hS Y.1 Y.2) (σ : N.sections) :
    modulePullbackSections B S hS g N σ = (globalSectionsPullbackMap B S hS g N).hom σ := by
  refine (SheafOfModules.unitHomEquiv _).symm.injective ?_
  refine ((SheafOfModules.unitHomEquiv _).symm_apply_apply _).trans ?_
  exact (unitHomEquiv_symm_globalSectionsPullbackMap g N σ).symm

/-- The ideal generated by the values of the linear functionals at an element does not change
along a linear equivalence. -/
theorem span_range_dual_apply_eq_of_linearEquiv {R M M' : Type*} [CommRing R] [AddCommGroup M]
    [Module R M] [AddCommGroup M'] [Module R M'] (E : M ≃ₗ[R] M') (m : M) :
    Ideal.span (Set.range fun l : Module.Dual R M => l m) =
      Ideal.span {a : R | ∃ φ : M' →ₗ[R] R, a = φ (E m)} := by
  apply le_antisymm
  · refine Ideal.span_le.2 ?_
    rintro a ⟨l, rfl⟩
    refine Ideal.subset_span ⟨l ∘ₗ E.symm.toLinearMap, ?_⟩
    simp
  · refine Ideal.span_le.2 ?_
    rintro a ⟨φ, rfl⟩
    exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨φ ∘ₗ E.toLinearMap, rfl⟩

/-- **The identity-chart case.** For an invertible module `N` on the algebraic space represented by
an affine scheme `T` and a global section `τ`, the ideal of global functions cut out on `T` by the
zero scheme of `τ` is generated by the values of the linear functionals on the global sections of
the chart restriction of `N` at the identity chart, at the restriction of `τ`. -/
theorem chartKer_zeroScheme_idEtaleChart_ideal_top (T : BigFppfOver B S hS) [IsAffine ((𝒯).obj T)]
    (N : Modules.{u, u} B S hS (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T).1
      (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T).2)
    (hN : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible
      (structureCommRings B S hS (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T))
      (structureRingSheaf B S hS (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T)).property N)
    (τ : N.sections) :
    haveI : IsAffine ((𝒯).obj (idEtaleChart B S hS T).1.left) := ‹IsAffine ((𝒯).obj T)›
    (chartKer B S hS (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T)
        (zeroScheme B S hS (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T) N τ)
        (idEtaleChart B S hS T).1.hom).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ =
      Ideal.span {a | ∃ φ : Γ(chartRestrictionSheaf B S hS (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T) N
          (idEtaleChart B S hS T), ⊤) →ₗ[Γ(chartScheme (idEtaleChart B S hS T), ⊤)]
            Γ(chartScheme (idEtaleChart B S hS T), ⊤),
        a = φ (chartRestrictionSheafTopEquiv B S hS (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T) N
          (idEtaleChart B S hS T) (τ.1 (op (idEtaleChart B S hS T))))} := by
  have hA : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T).1 ⋙
      BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (idEtaleChart B S hS T)) := ‹IsAffine ((𝒯).obj T)›
  have h3 := ker_chartBaseChangeHom B S hS (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T)
    (zeroScheme B S hS (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T) N τ) (idEtaleChart B S hS T) hA
  obtain ⟨Z, hZ⟩ := exists_definingIdealAt_eq_sectionEvaluationIdealAt_of_isInvertible B S hS
    (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T) N τ hN
  have h4 := definingIdealAt_zeroScheme_eq B S hS (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T) N τ Z hZ
    (idEtaleChart B S hS T) hA
  have h5 := ((chartKer_eq B S hS (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T) _ _).trans h3).trans
    (congrArg _ h4)
  have : IsAffine (chartScheme (idEtaleChart B S hS T)) := ‹IsAffine ((𝒯).obj T)›
  have : IsAffine ((𝒯).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T).1).obj
    (idEtaleChart B S hS T))) := ‹IsAffine ((𝒯).obj T)›
  refine (congrArg (fun I => Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal I ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) h5).trans ?_
  refine (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop_ideal _ _).trans ?_
  simp only [homOfLE_refl, op_id, CategoryTheory.Functor.map_id, CommRingCat.hom_id]
  refine (Ideal.map_id _).trans ?_
  exact @span_range_dual_apply_eq_of_linearEquiv _ _ _ _ _ (moduleChartSections B S hS _ N _) _ _
    (chartRestrictionSheafTopEquiv B S hS (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T) N
      (idEtaleChart B S hS T)) (τ.1 (op (idEtaleChart B S hS T)))

/-- **The chart ideal of a zero scheme along a scheme point, on an affine scheme.** For an
invertible `𝒪_X`-module `M`, a global section `σ` and `k : h_T ⟶ X` with `T` affine, the ideal of
global functions of the closed subscheme `Z(σ) ×_X T ⊆ T` is generated by the values of the linear
functionals on the global sections of the reading of `M` along `k` at the reading of `σ`. -/
theorem chartKer_zeroScheme_ideal_top_eq {X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS}
    (M : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2)
    (hM : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible (structurePresheaf B S hS X.1)
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS X.1 X.2).O)).property M)
    (σ : M.sections) (T : BigFppfOver B S hS) [IsAffine ((𝒯).obj T)]
    (k : representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T ⟶ X) :
    (chartKer B S hS X (zeroScheme B S hS X M σ) k.hom).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ =
      Ideal.span {a | ∃ φ : Γ(pointModule B S hS M T k, ⊤) →ₗ[Γ((𝒯).obj T, ⊤)] Γ((𝒯).obj T, ⊤),
        a = φ (pointGlobalSection B S hS M T k σ)} := by
  have hMag : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible (structureCommRings B S hS X)
      (structureRingSheaf B S hS X).property M :=
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible.toAlgebraicGeometry.{u, u + 1, u} _ _ _ hM
  have hN : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible
      (structureCommRings B S hS (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T))
      (structureRingSheaf B S hS (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T)).property
      ((modulePullback B S hS k).obj M) :=
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible.toAlgebraicGeometry.{u, u + 1, u} _ _ _
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isInvertible_pullbackModules_obj
        (f := smallEtaleRingedToposModulesHom B S hS k) (L := M) (hL := hM))
  have h2 : preimageSubspace B S hS k (zeroScheme B S hS X M σ) =
      zeroScheme B S hS (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T) ((modulePullback B S hS k).obj M)
        (modulePullbackSections B S hS k M σ) :=
    (zeroScheme_modulePullback_eq_preimage B S hS k M σ hMag).symm
  have h1 : chartKer B S hS X (zeroScheme B S hS X M σ) k.hom =
      chartKer B S hS (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T)
        (zeroScheme B S hS (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T) ((modulePullback B S hS k).obj M)
          (modulePullbackSections B S hS k M σ)) (idEtaleChart B S hS T).1.hom := by
    rw [← h2]
    refine Eq.trans ?_ (chartKer_preimage B S hS k (zeroScheme B S hS X M σ)
      (idEtaleChart B S hS T) k.hom (𝟙 T) (by simp [idEtaleChart])).symm
    exact (Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap_id _).symm
  have h3 := chartKer_zeroScheme_idEtaleChart_ideal_top B S hS T ((modulePullback B S hS k).obj M)
    hN (modulePullbackSections B S hS k M σ)
  have hb := modulePullbackSections_eq_globalSectionsPullbackMap B S hS k M σ
  refine (congrArg (·.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) h1).trans (h3.trans ?_)
  congr 1
  ext a
  exact exists_congr fun φ => by rw [hb]; rfl

/-- **Lemma R on an affine scheme.** The reading of `σ` along `k : h_T ⟶ X` vanishes at `t` exactly
when `t` lies in the closed subscheme `Z(σ) ×_X T`. -/
theorem mem_nonvanishingLocus_pointGlobalSection_iff_notMem_supportSet_chartKer_of_isAffine
    {X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS}
    (M : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2)
    (hM : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible (structurePresheaf B S hS X.1)
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS X.1 X.2).O)).property M)
    (σ : M.sections) (T : BigFppfOver B S hS) [IsAffine ((𝒯).obj T)]
    (k : representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T ⟶ X) (t : (𝒯).obj T) :
    t ∈ Stacks.Ample.nonvanishingLocus (pointModule B S hS M T k)
        (pointGlobalSection B S hS M T k σ) ↔
      t ∉ (chartKer B S hS X (zeroScheme B S hS X M σ) k.hom).supportSet := by
  have hA := isInvertibleModule_pointModule B S hS M hM T k
  have hB : SheafOfModules.IsInvertible ((𝒯).obj T).sheaf.obj ((𝒯).obj T).ringCatSheaf.property
      (pointModule B S hS M T k) :=
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isInvertible_iff_algebraicGeometry _ _ _).1 hA
  have heq : chartKer B S hS X (zeroScheme B S hS X M σ) k.hom =
      AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme ((𝒯).obj T) (pointModule B S hS M T k)
        (pointGlobalSection B S hS M T k σ) := by
    refine Scheme.IdealSheafData.ext_of_isAffine ?_
    refine (chartKer_zeroScheme_ideal_top_eq B S hS M hM σ T k).trans ?_
    refine Eq.trans ?_ (zeroScheme_ideal ((𝒯).obj T) (pointModule B S hS M T k)
      (pointGlobalSection B S hS M T k σ) ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩).symm
    simp only [homOfLE_refl, op_id, CategoryTheory.Functor.map_id, ConcreteCategory.id_apply]
  rw [heq]
  exact mem_nonvanishingLocus_iff_notMem_supportSet_zeroScheme _ _ t

/-- **The reading of a section vanishes exactly on the base change of its zero scheme.** For an
invertible `𝒪_X`-module `M`, a global section `σ`, a scheme `T` of the site and `k : h_T ⟶ X`, a
point `t ∈ T` lies in the nonvanishing locus of the reading of `σ` along `k` exactly when it lies
outside the closed subscheme `Z(σ) ×_X T` of `T`. -/
theorem mem_nonvanishingLocus_pointGlobalSection_iff_notMem_supportSet_chartKer
    {X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS}
    (M : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2)
    (hM : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible (structurePresheaf B S hS X.1)
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS X.1 X.2).O)).property M)
    (σ : M.sections) (T : BigFppfOver B S hS)
    (k : representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T ⟶ X) (t : (𝒯).obj T) :
    t ∈ Stacks.Ample.nonvanishingLocus (pointModule B S hS M T k)
        (pointGlobalSection B S hS M T k σ) ↔
      t ∉ (chartKer B S hS X (zeroScheme B S hS X M σ) k.hom).supportSet := by
  have hqc : M.IsQuasicoherentOnSite := isQuasicoherentOnSite_of_isInvertible B S hS X M
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible.toAlgebraicGeometry.{u, u + 1, u} _ _ _ hM)
  obtain ⟨W, hW, htW, -⟩ := exists_isAffineOpen_mem_and_subset (X := (𝒯).obj T) (x := t)
    (U := ⊤) trivial
  have : IsAffine (W : Scheme.{u}) := hW
  have hcW : B.Contains (W : Scheme.{u}) :=
    BigFppfSite.contains_of_locallyOfFinitePresentation B W.ι T.left.property
  let TW : BigFppfOver B S hS := BigFppfOver.siteObjectOver B S hS T hcW W.ι
  let r : TW ⟶ T := BigFppfOver.siteMapOver B S hS T hcW W.ι
  have hr : (𝒯).map r = W.ι := rfl
  have : IsAffine ((𝒯).obj TW) := hW
  let t' : (𝒯).obj TW := (⟨t, htW⟩ : (W : Scheme.{u}))
  have ht' : (𝒯).map r t' = t := rfl
  have h1 := mem_nonvanishingLocus_pointGlobalSection_iff B S hS M hqc r k
    (representedMap B S hS r ≫ k) rfl σ t'
  have h2 := mem_nonvanishingLocus_pointGlobalSection_iff_notMem_supportSet_chartKer_of_isAffine
    B S hS M hM σ TW
    (representedMap B S hS r ≫ k) t'
  have h3 := comap_chartKer B S hS X (zeroScheme B S hS X M σ) k.hom r
    (representedMap B S hS r ≫ k).hom rfl
  rw [ht'] at h1
  rw [← h1, h2, ← h3]
  change t' ∉ (((chartKer B S hS X (zeroScheme B S hS X M σ) k.hom).comap
    ((𝒯).map r)).support : Set _) ↔
      t ∉ ((chartKer B S hS X (zeroScheme B S hS X M σ) k.hom).support : Set _)
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_comap]
  rfl

/-- **The reading of a section vanishes exactly over the points of its zero scheme.** For an
invertible `𝒪_X`-module `M`, a global section `σ` and `k : h_T ⟶ X`, the reading of `σ` along `k`
vanishes at `t ∈ T` exactly when the image of `t` in `|X|` lies in `|Z(σ)|`. -/
theorem notMem_nonvanishingLocus_pointGlobalSection_iff_mem_subspacePointSet
    {X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS} (M : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2)
    (hM : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible (structurePresheaf B S hS X.1)
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS X.1 X.2).O)).property M)
    (σ : M.sections) (T : BigFppfOver B S hS)
    (k : representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T ⟶ X) (t : (𝒯).obj T) :
    t ∉ Stacks.Ample.nonvanishingLocus (pointModule B S hS M T k)
        (pointGlobalSection B S hS M T k σ) ↔
      pointsMap B S hS (yoneda.obj T) k.hom
          (presheafPoint B S hS T t (B.residueField_spec_contains T.left.property t)) ∈
        subspacePointSet B S hS X.1 (zeroScheme B S hS X M σ).1 := by
  rw [mem_nonvanishingLocus_pointGlobalSection_iff_notMem_supportSet_chartKer B S hS M hM σ T k t,
    not_not,
    ← image_preimage_subspacePointSet_eq_supportSet_chartKer B S hS X (zeroScheme B S hS X M σ)
      k.hom]
  refine ⟨fun ⟨p, hp, hpt⟩ => ?_, fun h => ⟨_, h, pointsToScheme_presheafPoint B S hS T t _⟩⟩
  rwa [← injective_pointsToScheme B S hS T
    (hpt.trans (pointsToScheme_presheafPoint B S hS T t _).symm)]

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
